The National People's Congress is like the **biggest school assembly** in China, but for grown-ups.

Imagine your school has a rule that everyone must wear a red coat on Fridays. Before that rule can happen, all the teachers and headteachers from every school in the whole country get together in one giant hall. They talk about the rule, they vote on it, and if most of them say "yes," then it becomes a rule for everyone.

In China, the National People's Congress is that giant hall. It's a meeting of thousands of people chosen from all over China. They get together to talk about the most important things for the whole country—like how to build new roads, how to keep the air clean, and how to make sure children have good schools. They also choose the person who is the main leader of the country.

So, if you think of China as a giant school, the National People's Congress is the special assembly where the most important grown-ups decide the big rules for everyone. [end of text]


